  "behavior": [
    "Existing Code/Keyboard continuity, sparse physical-channel edits, common-instrument edits and sound loads were already implemented and were verified. They retain the same loop/context/session and one HuC6280 Worklet.",
    "Code view now accepts performance keys after focus leaves the editor. Native text/select/dialog controls, contenteditable, Monaco/editor-host descendants, modifier shortcuts and already-handled key events are protected. The visible Keyboard panel still supports pointer keys.",
    "Manual Pitch captures engine/session/epoch and Code running state before queued dispatch. A stale operation or response cannot address a restarted session, replacement output or newly started song. Code start/stop and manual channel/Octave cleanup center the Pitch display.",
    "Keyboard cleanup scans owned slots, including released Software Envelope tails that are no longer in the held-note map. Code-owned notes and release tails remain active.",
    "When the final DDA feeder ends, simultaneous Wave/Noise voices keep the ordinary 16-frame Software Envelope clock. Actual WASM renders now match across whole and fragmented output blocks.",
    "Existing ownership policy is retained: older Code noteOff/keyOff does not silence a newer hand note; a later Code noteOn/keyOn takes ownership. Code frequency changes survive manual Pitch recentering.",
    "Noise, hardware LFO and DDA hand voices coexist with Code. Explicit Stop still fades to silence, invalidates old clients and restores the authored instrument.",
    "VGM manual editing is deferred. Existing VGM transport, paused audition/Capture, output mixer, Seek and exact checkpoint cache remain valid."
  ],
